enum: api.value 6:9 [Secret/probe] ($.spec.type) value is not one of the permitted choices: opaque, token, usernamePassword, dockerConfigJson, caBundle, tlsCertificate, sshKeyPair; next: use one of the permitted values
case-only enum: api.value 6:9 [Secret/probe] ($.spec.type) value is not one of the permitted choices: opaque, token, usernamePassword, dockerConfigJson, caBundle, tlsCertificate, sshKeyPair; next: use sshKeyPair (values are case-sensitive)
range: api.value 7:31 [Secret/probe] ($.spec.source.generated.bytes) number must be between 16 and 1024; next: use a value in that range
quoted integer: api.type 7:31 [Secret/probe] ($.spec.source.generated.bytes) expected integer, found string; a quoted value is a string; next: remove the quotes
quoted boolean: api.type 5:18 [Machine/probe] ($.spec.os.provided) expected boolean, found string; a quoted value is a string; next: remove the quotes
plain number in a string field: api.type 9:37 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.sites[0].description) expected string, found number; next: quote the value
missing reference: api.reference 9:37 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.remoteMachinesAccessKey.keyRef) no Secret named missing is in the selected input; next: declare Secret/missing, add its file to the selection, or correct the reference
wrong Secret type: api.reference 9:37 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.remoteMachinesAccessKey.keyRef) Secret/probe is declared as opaque; this field accepts sshKeyPair; next: reference a Secret of an accepted type or change Secret/probe's type
typo key: api.field 6:3 [Secret/probe] ($.spec.typ) unknown field; spec permits type, source; next: rename it to type
nested typo: api.field 8:5 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.domains.basee) unknown field; spec.domains permits base, machines, clusters, containerClusters, storageClusters; next: rename it to base
non-identifier key: api.field 7:3 [Secret/probe] ($.spec) a field name that is not a schema identifier is not permitted here; next: remove the field
kind defaults key: api.field 10:5 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.defaults.Machines) kind defaults name no registered kind; next: rename it to Machine
two Secret source arms: api.invariant 7:11 [Secret/probe] ($.spec.source) set at most one of contextStore, file, generated; next: keep one of them and remove the others
Proxy implementation enum: api.value 7:19 [Proxy/probe] ($.spec.implementation) value is not one of the permitted choices: squid; next: use one of the permitted values
Context document: api.kind 2:7 ($.kind) a Context is a standalone context configuration document, not desired state; next: keep it outside the input directory and pass it to context init or context update with -f
machineAccess: api.field 9:3 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.machineAccess) Environment machineAccess is retired; use spec.remoteMachinesAccessKey.keyRef; next: remove the retired field
safety: api.field 9:3 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.safety) Environment safety is retired; authorize data loss per command with --authorize data-loss on apply or destroy; next: remove the retired field
no Environment: api.invariant - exactly one Environment is required; next: add an Environment document, or pass the file that declares it with the others
two Environments: api.invariant 0:0 [Environment/synthetic] exactly one Environment is required; next: keep one Environment in the input and move the others out
two Environments: api.invariant 0:0 [Environment/second] exactly one Environment is required; next: keep one Environment in the input and move the others out
empty required list: api.value 6:18 [LoadBalancer/probe] ($.spec.bindAddresses) list must contain at least one entry; next: add at least one entry
duplicate entry: api.duplicate 9:25 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.sites[1]) entry repeats an earlier entry named east; next: remove or rename the repeated entry
duplicate entry that is not a label: api.value 9:18 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.sites[0].name) value does not match the required name grammar; next: write a value in the name grammar its field documents
duplicate entry that is not a label: api.duplicate 9:42 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.sites[1]) entry repeats an earlier entry; next: remove or rename the repeated entry
duplicate entry that is not a label: api.value 9:49 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.sites[1].name) value does not match the required name grammar; next: write a value in the name grammar its field documents
name that is not a label: api.field 7:3 ($.spec.typ) unknown field; spec permits type, source; next: rename it to type
name that is not a label, alone: api.value 4:9 ($.metadata.name) Secret metadata.name must be a lowercase DNS label; next: rename it to a lowercase DNS label of at most 63 characters, letters a-z, digits and '-', starting and ending with a letter or digit, and rename every reference to it
Machine name that is not a label: api.value 3:18 ($.metadata.name) Machine metadata.name must be a lowercase DNS label; next: rename it to a lowercase DNS label of at most 63 characters, letters a-z, digits and '-', starting and ending with a letter or digit, and rename every reference to it
key three edits from its only near field: api.field 6:3 [Secret/probe] ($.spec.name) unknown field; spec permits type, source; next: remove it or use a permitted field
kind three edits from a registered kind: api.kind 2:7 ($.kind) kind must name a registered API kind; next: use a registered kind name
kind defaults key three edits from a kind: api.field 10:5 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.defaults.Mach) kind defaults name no registered kind; next: use a registered kind name such as Machine
referenced Secret that does not decode: api.field 7:3 [Secret/probe] ($.spec.extra) unknown field; spec permits type, source; next: remove it or use a permitted field
referenced Secret whose type is not a string: api.type 6:9 [Secret/probe] ($.spec.type) expected string, found integer; next: quote the value
network selection without a configured network: api.required 5:3 [Machine/probe] ($.spec.os) required field is absent; next: add os (mapping)
network selection without a configured network: api.invariant 6:24 [Machine/probe] ($.spec.network.installAddressRef) network selections and bindings require a configured network; next: select a network configuration on Machine/probe with spec.network.configRef or spec.network.inline, or remove spec.network.installAddressRef
network selection without a configured network: api.invariant 7:62 [Machine/probe] ($.spec.network.addresses[0].interface) interface assignment requires a non-provided Machine with configured network; next: select a network configuration on Machine/probe with spec.network.configRef or spec.network.inline, or remove spec.network.addresses[0].interface
interface assignment on an OS-ready Machine: api.invariant 7:62 [Machine/probe] ($.spec.network.addresses[0].interface) interface assignment requires a non-provided Machine with configured network; next: remove spec.network.addresses[0].interface from Machine/probe; an OS-ready Machine declares contacts only
selected cluster that does not decode: api.field 5:3 [ContainerCluster/probe] ($.spec.extra) unknown field; spec permits distribution, install, networking, security, nodes; next: remove it or use a permitted field
OS-ready Machine with installation declarations: api.required 6:3 [Environment/synthetic] ($.spec.remoteMachinesAccessKey.keyRef) Machine/probe installs a managed OS and needs the fleet SSH key; next: set spec.remoteMachinesAccessKey.keyRef to an sshKeyPair Secret
OS-ready Machine with installation declarations: api.invariant 5:43 [Machine/probe] ($.spec.os.installProfileRef) OS-ready Machines forbid installation declarations; next: remove spec.os.installProfileRef, or set spec.os.provided to false for a Machine Bootwright installs
OS-ready Machine with installation declarations: api.reference 5:43 [Machine/probe] ($.spec.os.installProfileRef) no MachineInstallProfile named rhel is in the selected input; next: declare MachineInstallProfile/rhel, add its file to the selection, or correct the reference
OS-ready Machine with a network configuration: api.invariant 6:24 [Machine/probe] ($.spec.network.configRef) OS-ready Machines declare contacts only; next: remove spec.network.configRef; an OS-ready Machine declares contacts only
OS-ready Machine with a network configuration: api.reference 6:24 [Machine/probe] ($.spec.network.configRef) no NetworkConfig named net is in the selected input; next: declare NetworkConfig/net, add its file to the selection, or correct the reference
non-provided Machine without a provider: api.invariant 5:3 [Machine/probe] ($.spec.substrate.providerRef) non-provided Machines require a substrate provider; next: set spec.substrate.providerRef to the InfraProvider that realizes this Machine, or set spec.os.provided to true for a Machine whose OS is already installed
